  "format": "doorprints-india-place-vectors/1",
  "note": "Towns and places across India with whether they lie inside the held areas, the polygon of web/public/geo/in-held-areas.geojson (and its byte-identical Android copy) inside which the app leaves the Pakistani and Chinese admin lines out of the map (docs/03 ADR-22, S4b-BL-12). heldBy names the administration whose lines are left out; a place without it is in India as the Government of India depicts it, and its admin lines are drawn. Coordinates are the public locations of the towns; Uri, Poonch, Kargil, Dras and Turtuk lie 4 to 9 km from the polygon of the held areas. Read by web india-boundaries.spec.ts (the style filter, with MapLibre's own evaluator) and Android IndiaBoundaryDataTest (the polygon), so both apps decide every place alike. The boundary data itself is not changed by this file. S4b-BL-174c adds two lists read by the place lookup of both apps (web place-search.spec.ts, Android PlaceLookupTest): borderTowns are places of India close to a border that a lookup must keep, and abroad are towns of the neighbours, most of them inside India's bounding box, that a lookup must refuse. Every entry of places and of borderTowns is inside the outline of India as the Government of India depicts it (web/src/app/shared/india-outline.geojson, built by web/scripts/geo/build_in_outline.py from the same boundary data) and every entry of abroad is outside it.",
